      "Practice Level 0 Definition": "1. You are not aware of what makes up the practice\n1. You are not willing to practice it\n1. You tried to practice it, but stopped",
      "Practice Level 1 Definition": "1. You believe it's valuable to practice the practice\n1. You are willing to practice it\n1. You have knowledge about the components of the practice\n1. You've started practicing with others and reflecting",
      "Practice Level 2 Definition": "1. You've seen growth in your own practice through reflection\n1. You are starting to work on changing habits",
      "Practice Level 3 Definition": "1. Your habits are starting to become automatic in your practice with others\n1. You’re so practiced in it, that you are a role model to others in the practice\n1. You can and do advocate for the practice when working with others",
