          "label": "Tech Fleet Sprint Demo Slide Deck Template"
        }
      ],
      "What Mindset Do You Have When You Practice This Practice?": "Continuous Improvement comes from believing that growth is always possible and that failure is a lesson rather than a verdict. You see feedback as a gift that shows you where to get better, and you pay attention to how your own actions affect the people around you.",
      "What Habits Do You Hold When You Practice This Practice?": "This shows up when you regularly step back to reflect on how things went, seek out feedback and act on it instead of getting defensive, and treat fast failures as chances to learn. You watch your own impact on others and make small, steady changes to how you work.",
      "Practice Description": "Continuous Improvement is the habit of a team getting a little better all the time by reflecting honestly and acting on what it learns. Instead of repeating the same mistakes, the team treats every sprint and every setback as a chance to adjust how it works. It grows from habits like reflection, self-awareness, seeking feedback, and failing fast. Over time, small improvements add up to a team that keeps getting stronger.",
      "Where Can I Learn More?": "Atlassian Team Playbook, practical plays for healthy teamwork: https://www.atlassian.com/team-playbook"
    }
  ]
}